<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Indra Jatra</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Yenya</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indra">Indra</a> Jatra is an annual festival in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathmandu">Kathmandu</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a>, held in late summer or early autumn in honour of the god Indra. Celebrated above all by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newar-people">Newar people</a>, it includes the raising of a ceremonial pole, masked dances and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chariot">chariot</a> procession of the living goddess Kumari, who blesses the head of state. The forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prithvi-narayan-shah">Prithvi Narayan Shah</a> took Kathmandu during the festival in 1768.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/indra-jatra.jpg" alt="Indra Jatra" width="320" height="410" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kamal Ratna Tuladhar · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sweta_bhairava_krt.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
